<section id="help" class="page hidden"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Here when you need it</span><h2>Tech help</h2><p>Plain-language guides for everyday questions.</p></div></div><div class="card"><h3>Choose a topic</h3><details class="help-item"><summary>How do I make text bigger on my phone?</summary><p>Open your phone’s Settings. Look for Display or Accessibility, then choose Text size or Display size. Move the slider until the words feel comfortable. The exact names can vary by phone.</p></details><details class="help-item"><summary>How do I make a video call?</summary><p>Open the video calling app you already use, such as FaceTime or WhatsApp. Choose a person from your contacts and tap the video camera symbol. You may need to allow access to your camera and microphone.</p></details><details class="help-item"><summary>What if a message asks me to send money?</summary><p>Pause before clicking or sending anything. Contact the person or organization using a phone number you already trust, not a number in the message. Never share passwords or one-time security codes.</p></details><details class="help-item"><summary>How do I connect to Wi-Fi?</summary><p>Open Settings, choose Wi-Fi, and select the name of your network. Enter its password if asked. On some phones, you can also hold the Wi-Fi symbol in the quick settings panel.</p></details></div></section><footer>Made for the little moments in your day. &nbsp;·&nbsp; My Day</footer></main><script src="{{ asset('js/my-day.js') }}" defer></script></body></html>

